# New blog article workflow

When adding a blog to `monash-wam-calculator`, follow this exact pattern.

## Featured image (required)

1. Create a **realistic photo-style** banner matching the article topic (16:9, editorial/stock look — not flat SVG gradients).
2. Save as `public/article-images/featured-{slug}.webp`.
3. Compress to **1280×720 WebP** (~50–200 KB). Run from repo root:
   ```bash
   node scripts/compress-featured-image.mjs featured-{slug}.jpg
   ```
   (Pass the source JPG/PNG filename if starting from a generated image.)
4. Set `featuredImage: '/article-images/featured-{slug}.webp'` in `articles.ts`.
5. Write `featuredImageAlt` — describe **what is in the photo** (students, laptop, campus, etc.). Never use “banner”, “illustration”, or color-theme-only text.
6. **Do not** add calculator iframe heroes. Cards and article pages both use `ArticleFeaturedImage` → same file, same alt.

## Article entry (`src/data/articles.ts`)

- Add full entry to `articles` array: slug, keyword, title, description, featuredImage, featuredImageAlt, dates, sections, faqs.
- Include internal link phrases in body text for existing guides/calculators (max 2 auto-linked per article via `ArticlePost`).

## SEO wiring

1. Add URL to `public/sitemap.xml`:
   `https://monashwamcalculator.com/articles/{slug}`
2. If the primary keyword is new, add to `keywordInternalLinks` in `src/pages/ArticlePost.tsx`.
3. Cross-link from 1–2 related existing articles in paragraph text.

## Do not

- Use `.svg` or multi-MB `.png`/`.jpg` for featured images in production.
- Use different images on `/articles` cards vs article header.
- Reintroduce `referenceEmbed` / iframe as the hero image.
- **Repeat a topic or primary keyword** already covered below. Each article must have one distinct search intent.

